WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:19.749
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is mono no aware: the petal falling. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.056
Feel the surface beneath you. Unclench your jaw. Let your shoulders settle. For these five minutes, there is nowhere else you need to be.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:08.031
Feel the quiet rhythm of breathing. When the mind moves ahead, come back to one simple inhale and one unhurried exhale.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:35.331
Mono no aware is the quiet ache at the heart of lovely things, because they do not stay. It is not grief. It is the tenderness that comes with paying attention.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:01.217
Blossom coming off a branch in a light wind. Nobody watching wishes it were plastic. The falling is not the flaw in the flower; it is the whole of it.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.031
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:56.824
Rest on the breath you are in. It is leaving as you hold it. You are not losing it. You are being present for it while it is here.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.913
For a little while, I will be quiet. Let thoughts pass like weather over a wide landscape. When attention wanders, return with patience.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.613
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:25.684
Let one ordinary thing register today as though it were rare. A face across a table. Light on a wall at a particular hour.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:52.195
Take one fuller breath. Feel the space beyond your body and let your eyes open in their own time. Thank you for practicing with Karma.
